$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n![](images/97/979b63f21e56924bd7880f9487cf829089e38cf14d287e70196c7a661e41f97f.png)\n\nMoreover, if $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, whereas statement II is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would not rotate. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ the vector field $F$ is irrotational.\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ it points in neither the positive nor the negative $z$-direction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241116 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133881 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d42243ea-58fc-53f6-a0b6-f995bf1d697c" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Curl of a Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "290a275b-f839-5d88-b09c-a1a161329cf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238417} {:answer/id #uuid "2b8cab37-88f1-56c5-a40e-bc46fb13b532" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238444} {:answer/id #uuid "66c4c8a7-c323-50f9-b54e-723343686c81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :ans